#: src/features/legal/texts/HowPowrDecides.tsx
msgid "Every number POWR uses is a value in one versioned list, the rules registry. Each value names its evidence and its sources, so any suggestion can be traced back. Where research gives a clear answer, POWR uses it. Where research is thin, it uses an established coaching convention, and where neither gives a number, its own estimate, labelled as such."
msgstr "Every number POWR uses is a value in one versioned list, the rules registry. Each value names its evidence and its sources, so any suggestion can be traced back. Where research gives a clear answer, POWR uses it. Where research is thin, it uses an established coaching convention, and where neither gives a number, its own estimate, labelled as such."

#: src/features/legal/texts/Privacy.tsx
msgid "Everything you enter is stored only on this device. We never receive it: there is no account, analytics or tracking. Only you can export it, as a backup file."
msgstr "Everything you enter is stored only on this device. We never receive it: there is no account, analytics or tracking. Only you can export it, as a backup file."

#: src/features/legal/texts/HowPowrDecides.tsx
msgid "Exercise library and templates: {contentVersion}"
msgstr "Exercise library and templates: {contentVersion}"

#: src/features/legal/texts/HowPowrDecides.tsx
msgid "From the weight, reps and effort of your sets, POWR estimates the most you could lift once (your estimated 1-rep max). Heavy, hard sets count most. The trend is smoothed, because single workouts vary by several percent; a change is only called likely real once it is larger than that day-to-day variation and lasts for a few workouts."
msgstr "From the weight, reps and effort of your sets, POWR estimates the most you could lift once (your estimated 1-rep max). Heavy, hard sets count most. The trend is smoothed, because single workouts vary by several percent; a change is only called likely real once it is larger than that day-to-day variation and lasts for a few workouts."

